1. INTRODUCTION


1.1 Purpose

The purpose of this Software Requirements Specification (SRS) document is to define the functional and non-functional requirements of the Cybersecurity Awareness Platform for Phishing Detection and Prevention.

This document describes the features, functionality, system behaviour, interfaces, constraints, and quality requirements of the proposed system.

The Cybersecurity Awareness Platform is designed to improve users' understanding of cybersecurity threats, particularly phishing attacks. The system will provide educational training content, safe phishing simulations, interactive quizzes, performance assessment, progress tracking, and feedback.

This SRS document will serve as a reference for the project team during the design, development, testing, and maintenance of the system.


1.2 Document Conventions

The following conventions are used in this SRS document:

• Section headings are numbered according to the structure of the SRS document.

• Functional requirements are identified using unique requirement identifiers such as REQ-1, REQ-2, and so on.

• The word "shall" indicates a mandatory system requirement.

• The word "should" indicates a recommended requirement.

• The terms User, Administrator, System, Training Module, Simulation Module, and Quiz Module are used consistently throughout the document.

• Requirements are organized into functional and non-functional categories for clarity and traceability.


1.3 Intended Audience and Reading Suggestions

This SRS document is intended for the following stakeholders:

Project Team:
The project team will use this document to understand the project requirements and guide the design and development of the system.

Team Leader:
The Team Leader will use this document for project planning, requirement management, task coordination, and project monitoring.

Developer:
The Developer will use this document to understand the functional requirements, system features, technical constraints, and software interfaces required for implementation.

Tester:
The Tester will use this document to prepare test cases and verify whether the implemented system satisfies the specified requirements.

Administrator:
The Administrator will use the system to manage users, training content, quizzes, and other administrative activities.

End Users:
End users will use the platform to access cybersecurity training, participate in phishing simulations, attempt quizzes, and view their performance and progress.

The recommended reading sequence is to first read the Introduction and Overall Description sections to understand the system. Developers and testers should then review the External Interface Requirements and System Features. All stakeholders should review the Nonfunctional Requirements.


1.4 Product Scope

The Cybersecurity Awareness Platform for Phishing Detection and Prevention is a web-based software system designed to improve cybersecurity awareness among users.

The primary purpose of the system is to educate users about phishing attacks and help them identify suspicious emails, malicious links, fake websites, and other common phishing techniques.

The proposed system will provide the following major features:

• Secure user registration and authentication.

• Cybersecurity awareness training material.

• Information about phishing attacks and phishing techniques.

• Safe and educational phishing simulations.

• Interactive cybersecurity quizzes.

• Quiz result calculation and performance assessment.

• Feedback based on user performance.

• Progress tracking.

• Administrative management of training content and quizzes.

The system aims to provide a practical and interactive learning environment that improves users' ability to recognize phishing attempts and follow safe online practices.

The system does not perform real phishing attacks, malware removal, antivirus scanning, network intrusion detection, or digital forensic investigation.


1.5 References

The following references were used while preparing this Software Requirements Specification:

1. Software Requirements Specification template provided in the Software Engineering course material.

2. Experiment 2: Problem Identification and Feasibility for the Cybersecurity Awareness Platform for Phishing Detection and Prevention.

3. Experiment 3: Stakeholder Identification and Requirement Elicitation for the Cybersecurity Awareness Platform for Phishing Detection and Prevention.

4. Project requirements and stakeholder requirements identified by the project team.






2. OVERALL DESCRIPTION


2.1 Product Perspective

The Cybersecurity Awareness Platform for Phishing Detection and Prevention is a web-based software application designed to provide cybersecurity education and practical awareness training to users.

The system will function as an independent web application that allows users to access cybersecurity learning materials, participate in phishing simulations, attempt quizzes, receive feedback, and monitor their learning progress.

The proposed system consists of multiple modules that work together to provide an effective learning environment.

The major components of the system include:

• User Authentication Module

• Cybersecurity Awareness Training Module

• Phishing Simulation Module

• Quiz and Assessment Module

• Performance Tracking Module

• Feedback Module

• Administrative Management Module


The User Authentication Module will allow users to register and securely log in to the system.

The Cybersecurity Awareness Training Module will provide educational content related to cybersecurity threats, phishing attacks, suspicious emails, malicious links, fake websites, and safe online practices.

The Phishing Simulation Module will provide safe and educational scenarios that allow users to practice identifying phishing attempts.

The Quiz and Assessment Module will allow users to attempt interactive questions and evaluate their cybersecurity knowledge.

The Performance Tracking Module will store and display user performance and learning progress.

The Feedback Module will provide appropriate feedback to users based on their quiz and simulation performance.

The Administrative Management Module will allow administrators to manage training content, quiz questions, and other system-related information.

The system is designed using a modular approach so that new features can be added in the future without significantly affecting the existing system.


2.2 Product Functions

The Cybersecurity Awareness Platform will provide the following major functions:

1. User Registration

The system shall allow new users to register and create an account.


2. User Login and Authentication

The system shall allow registered users to securely log in using valid credentials.


3. Cybersecurity Awareness Training

The system shall provide educational material related to cybersecurity and common online threats.


4. Phishing Awareness

The system shall provide information about phishing attacks, phishing techniques, suspicious emails, malicious links, and fake websites.


5. Phishing Simulation

The system shall provide safe phishing simulation scenarios to help users practice identifying phishing attempts.


6. Interactive Quiz

The system shall provide cybersecurity-related quizzes to evaluate user knowledge.


7. Performance Assessment

The system shall calculate and display user performance based on quiz and simulation results.


8. Feedback

The system shall provide feedback to users based on their answers and performance.


9. Progress Tracking

The system shall allow users to view their learning progress and previous performance.


10. Administrative Management

The system shall allow administrators to manage training content, quiz questions, and other relevant system information.


2.3 User Classes and Characteristics

The Cybersecurity Awareness Platform will have different categories of users. Each user class will interact with the system according to its role and permissions.


2.3.1 End User

End users are the primary users of the system.

They may include students, regular internet users, and working professionals who want to improve their cybersecurity awareness.

End users will use the system to:

• Register and log in to the platform.

• Access cybersecurity awareness training material.

• Learn about phishing attacks.

• Participate in phishing simulations.

• Attempt cybersecurity quizzes.

• Receive feedback.

• View their performance.

• Monitor their learning progress.

End users are not required to have advanced technical knowledge. Therefore, the system should provide a simple, clear, and user-friendly interface.


2.3.2 Administrator

The administrator is responsible for managing the content and activities of the system.

The administrator will be able to:

• Manage training content.

• Add or update cybersecurity learning material.

• Manage quiz questions.

• Monitor relevant user activities.

• Maintain system information.

The administrator is expected to have basic knowledge of the system and its administrative functions.


2.3.3 Project Team

The project team consists of the Team Leader, Developer, and Tester.

The Team Leader is responsible for coordinating project activities and monitoring project progress.

The Developer is responsible for implementing the frontend, backend, database, and other technical components of the system.

The Tester is responsible for testing system features, identifying defects, and verifying whether the system meets the specified requirements.


2.4 Operating Environment

The Cybersecurity Awareness Platform will operate as a web-based application.

The system can be accessed using a computer or laptop with an internet connection and a supported web browser.

The expected operating environment includes:

Client Side:

• Windows, Linux, or other supported operating systems.

• Modern web browsers such as Google Chrome, Microsoft Edge, or Mozilla Firefox.

• Internet connection.


Server Side:

• Node.js runtime environment.

• Express.js for backend application development.

• MongoDB database for storing application data.


Development Environment:

• Visual Studio Code.

• Git for version control.

• GitHub for source code management and collaboration.

• Postman for API testing.


2.5 Design and Implementation Constraints

The development of the Cybersecurity Awareness Platform may be affected by the following constraints:


1. Time Constraint

The project must be completed within the time period specified for the academic project.


2. Resource Constraint

The project is being developed by a limited number of team members. Therefore, the available development time and resources are limited.


3. Technology Constraint

The system will be developed using the technologies selected by the project team.

The frontend and backend technologies should be compatible with each other and suitable for web application development.


4. Security Constraint

The system must follow appropriate security practices for user authentication and data handling.

User credentials and personal information should be handled securely.


5. Internet Dependency

Since the system is web-based, users require an internet connection to access the application.


6. Simulation Safety Constraint

The phishing simulations provided by the system must be educational and safe.

The system must not perform actual phishing attacks or send malicious content to users.


2.6 User Documentation

The Cybersecurity Awareness Platform should provide appropriate documentation and guidance for users.

The user documentation may include:

• Instructions for user registration and login.

• Guidelines for accessing cybersecurity training material.

• Instructions for participating in phishing simulations.

• Instructions for attempting quizzes.

• Information about viewing performance and progress.

• Administrator guidelines for managing training content and quizzes.

The documentation should use simple and clear language so that users with different levels of technical knowledge can understand the system.


2.7 Assumptions and Dependencies

The following assumptions are made during the development and operation of the Cybersecurity Awareness Platform:


Assumptions:

• Users have access to a computer or other supported device.

• Users have access to a stable internet connection.

• Users have basic knowledge of using a web browser.

• Users will provide valid information during registration.

• Administrators will manage training content and quiz information appropriately.

• Users will use the phishing simulation features only for educational purposes.


Dependencies:

• The system depends on the selected web development technologies.

• The system depends on the availability of the database for storing user and application data.

• The system depends on an internet connection for web-based access.

• The system depends on GitHub for source code management and team collaboration.

• The system may depend on third-party libraries and software packages required during development.

Future changes in technologies, software libraries, or database services may require modifications to the system.







