    4. SYSTEM FEATURES


4.1 User Authentication


4.1.1 Description and Priority

The User Authentication feature allows users to register and securely access the Cybersecurity Awareness Platform.

The system will allow new users to create an account and existing users to log in using valid credentials.

Authentication is required to provide personalized access to training content, quizzes, simulation activities, performance records, and learning progress.

Priority: High


4.1.2 Stimulus/Response Sequence

Stimulus:

The user enters the registration or login information and submits the request.

Response:

The system validates the provided information.

If the registration information is valid, the system creates a new user account.

If the login credentials are valid, the system grants access to the user dashboard.

If the information or credentials are invalid, the system displays an appropriate error message.


4.1.3 Functional Requirements

REQ-1: The system shall allow a new user to register and create an account.

REQ-2: The system shall validate the required information during user registration.

REQ-3: The system shall allow registered users to log in using valid credentials.

REQ-4: The system shall validate user credentials before granting access.

REQ-5: The system shall display an appropriate error message when invalid login credentials are provided.

REQ-6: The system shall provide authenticated users with access to their authorized features.

REQ-7: The system shall restrict unauthorized users from accessing protected features.


4.2 Cybersecurity Awareness Training


4.2.1 Description and Priority

The Cybersecurity Awareness Training feature provides educational content to improve users' understanding of cybersecurity threats and safe online practices.

The training module will provide information about cybersecurity fundamentals, phishing attacks, suspicious emails, malicious links, fake websites, password security, and other relevant cybersecurity topics.

The purpose of this feature is to provide users with clear and understandable cybersecurity awareness material.

Priority: High


4.2.2 Stimulus/Response Sequence

Stimulus:

The user selects a cybersecurity training topic.

Response:

The system retrieves the requested training content and displays it to the user.

The user can read and navigate through the available learning material.

The system may record the completion or progress of the training activity.


4.2.3 Functional Requirements

REQ-8: The system shall provide cybersecurity awareness training material.

REQ-9: The system shall organize training content into different cybersecurity topics.

REQ-10: The system shall provide information about common cybersecurity threats.

REQ-11: The system shall provide information about phishing attacks and phishing techniques.

REQ-12: The system shall provide information about suspicious emails and malicious links.

REQ-13: The system shall provide information about safe online practices.

REQ-14: The system shall allow users to access and navigate between available training topics.


4.3 Phishing Simulation


4.3.1 Description and Priority

The Phishing Simulation feature provides users with safe and educational scenarios that simulate common phishing attempts.

The purpose of this feature is to allow users to practice identifying suspicious emails, malicious links, fake websites, and other phishing indicators.

The simulations are intended only for cybersecurity education and awareness.

The system will not perform real phishing attacks or distribute malicious content.

Priority: High


4.3.2 Stimulus/Response Sequence

Stimulus:

The user selects a phishing simulation activity.

Response:

The system displays a simulated phishing scenario.

The user analyzes the provided information and identifies suspicious elements or selects an appropriate answer.

The system evaluates the user's response and displays appropriate feedback.


4.3.3 Functional Requirements

REQ-15: The system shall provide safe phishing simulation scenarios.

REQ-16: The system shall provide simulated examples of phishing emails.

REQ-17: The system shall provide simulated examples of suspicious or malicious links for educational purposes.

REQ-18: The system shall provide simulated examples of fake websites or suspicious web pages for educational purposes.

REQ-19: The system shall allow users to identify suspicious elements in a phishing scenario.

REQ-20: The system shall evaluate the user's response to a phishing simulation.

REQ-21: The system shall provide feedback based on the user's simulation performance.

REQ-22: The system shall ensure that all phishing simulations are educational and do not perform actual phishing attacks.


4.4 Quiz and Assessment


4.4.1 Description and Priority

The Quiz and Assessment feature allows users to evaluate their cybersecurity knowledge through interactive questions.

The quiz may include questions related to cybersecurity fundamentals, phishing attacks, suspicious emails, malicious links, fake websites, and safe online practices.

The system will evaluate user responses and calculate the quiz results.

Priority: High


4.4.2 Stimulus/Response Sequence

Stimulus:

The user selects a quiz and submits answers to the displayed questions.

Response:

The system records the user's answers.

After quiz submission, the system evaluates the answers.

The system calculates the user's score and displays the result.

The system provides appropriate feedback based on the user's performance.


4.4.3 Functional Requirements

REQ-23: The system shall provide cybersecurity-related quizzes.

REQ-24: The system shall display quiz questions to the user.

REQ-25: The system shall allow users to select or submit answers to quiz questions.

REQ-26: The system shall evaluate the submitted quiz answers.

REQ-27: The system shall calculate the user's quiz score.

REQ-28: The system shall display the quiz result to the user.

REQ-29: The system shall provide feedback based on the user's quiz performance.

REQ-30: The system shall store quiz results for future performance tracking.


4.5 Performance Tracking and Feedback


4.5.1 Description and Priority

The Performance Tracking and Feedback feature allows users to monitor their cybersecurity learning progress.

The system will store relevant quiz and simulation results and provide feedback based on the user's performance.

This feature helps users identify their strengths and areas that require improvement.

Priority: Medium


4.5.2 Stimulus/Response Sequence

Stimulus:

The user completes a quiz, training activity, or phishing simulation.

Response:

The system records the relevant performance information.

The system calculates or updates the user's progress.

The system displays performance information and appropriate feedback.

The user can view the available performance and progress records.


4.5.3 Functional Requirements

REQ-31: The system shall record relevant user performance information.

REQ-32: The system shall store quiz results.

REQ-33: The system shall store relevant phishing simulation results.

REQ-34: The system shall display the user's quiz performance.

REQ-35: The system shall display the user's simulation performance.

REQ-36: The system shall allow users to view their learning progress.

REQ-37: The system shall provide feedback based on user performance.

REQ-38: The system shall provide information that helps users identify areas for improvement.


4.6 Administrative Management


4.6.1 Description and Priority

The Administrative Management feature allows authorized administrators to manage important system content and information.

Administrators will be responsible for maintaining cybersecurity training material and quiz-related information.

This feature ensures that the educational content of the platform can be updated and maintained.

Priority: Medium


4.6.2 Stimulus/Response Sequence

Stimulus:

The administrator logs in and accesses the administrative functions.

Response:

The system verifies the administrator's authorization.

The system provides access to administrative features.

The administrator can manage training content and quiz-related information.

The system validates and stores the changes made by the administrator.


4.6.3 Functional Requirements

REQ-39: The system shall provide authorized administrators with access to administrative functions.

REQ-40: The system shall allow administrators to manage cybersecurity training content.

REQ-41: The system shall allow administrators to add new training material.

REQ-42: The system shall allow administrators to update existing training material.

REQ-43: The system shall allow administrators to manage quiz questions.

REQ-44: The system shall validate administrative changes before storing the updated information.

REQ-45: The system shall store and retrieve administrative content changes appropriately.





